From be25e56e411bbbed487b422b51d4db20aef83db6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "gastown.slit (polecat)" <polecat-gastown.slit@soundit.local>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 23:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: merge two clients into one (psa-cbr)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds staff-facing "merge duplicate client" for GitHub #171. On a client
detail page, staff pick another client to fold INTO the one they're viewing;
that client survives and the duplicate is soft-deleted.

ClientService::mergeClients() is the business logic, mirroring the existing
PersonService::mergePeople() pattern: one DB transaction, pessimistic lock on
both client rows, query-builder repoints (no model observers fire), and a raw
DB::table update so soft-deleted rows move too — nothing is left pointing at
the tombstoned client. It repoints every client-owned domain record (tickets,
assets, people, phone calls, emails, contracts, invoices, licenses),
re-parents the duplicate's reseller children, fills only the survivor's BLANK
profile fields from the duplicate (never overwrites), and writes an audit note
on both records.

Two non-obvious edges are handled explicitly:
- licenses carry a UNIQUE(license_type_id, client_id, vendor_ref) index, so a
  duplicate license that would collide with a survivor license on the same
  type + non-null vendor_ref is dropped as redundant rather than repointed
  (a NULL vendor_ref never collides and always moves).
- if the survivor was itself resold BY the duplicate, that reseller link is
  nulled so the survivor can't become its own reseller.

Scope boundary: auxiliary tables that merely reference a client (alerts,
ninja_alerts, the wiki knowledge base, technician/tooling-gap AI logs) are
intentionally NOT repointed — they are nullable monitoring/AI-log rows that
don't define client identity. Integration mapping IDs (Stripe/QBO/RMM/…) are
not carried over either; they retire with the duplicate and can be re-mapped.
Unlike deleteClient(), merge does not block on open tickets / active contracts
/ unpaid invoices — consolidating those is the whole point.

UI mirrors the person-merge modal: a guarded Merge button + confirm modal with
a candidate <select> on clients/show. Route: POST /clients/{client}/merge.

Validation: 15 new tests (ClientMergeServiceTest + ClientMergeTest) covering
core repoints, license collision/NULL handling, reseller re-parenting and the
self-reseller edge, blank-field fill, audit notes, the no-orphans invariant,
the self-merge guard, and the HTTP flow incl. the show-page modal render.
